{
  "schemaVersion": 3,
  "updated": "2026-09-18",
  "arbiter": {
    "decisionEngine": {
      "engine": "jev",
      "added": "2026-09-16",
      "model": "jev-latest",
      "endpoint": "https://api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone",
      "keyEnv": "TYPESAFE_API_KEY",
      "tools": [
        "tools/jev-client.js",
        "tools/jev-arbiter.js",
        "tools/jev-check.js"
      ],
      "gates": {
        "classifyRoute": 0.6,
        "classifyRouteFlagged": 0.4,
        "seatRoute": 0.6,
        "seatRouteFlagged": 0.4,
        "seatMinMarginToFlip": 0.15,
        "convene": 0.6,
        "netBenefit": 0.6,
        "independentEvidence": 0.6,
        "claimSupported": 0.6,
        "claimContradicted": 0.4
      },
      "policy": "Jev proposes distributions; deterministic code gates. The hosting session stays the driver and runs the tools; Jev reads no files and dispatches nothing. Seat picks come from mix-mode routing.json decisionMatrix2026-09-16 under the margin rule and never name a model whose capacity bucket is exhausted (docs/capacity-state.json). A missing TYPESAFE_API_KEY yields a NOT_RUN result, never a throw; every real call appends a provenance row (request and response sha256, usage, model, timestamp) and never the key. Seats do not call Jev; only the lead runs tools/jev-check.js over seat output, after deterministic pre-checks.",
      "provenance": "jev-decisions.jsonl in the run directory",
      "note": "The principles.arbiter* rows above are unchanged by this block; wiring the Jev classify result into plan-seal and retiring the xai arbiter check in tools/dispatch-matrix.js is a separate, owner-approved step."
    }
  },
  "principles": {
    "arbiterVendor": "jev",
    "arbiterModel": "jev-latest",
    "arbiterNeverSeat": true,
    "arbiterNeverImplements": true,
    "arbiterNeverReviews": true,
    "arbiterNeverVerifies": true,
    "arbiterNeverVotes": true,
    "deterministicRulesOutrankModels": true,
    "distributionFloor": 0.6,
    "distributionFloorMinimumImplementUnits": 2,
    "maxConcurrentDispatches": 3,
    "maxConcurrentDispatchesNote": "Owner question 2026-09-16 (\"adapt the head count max so we do not fan out too many agents once seats are active\"): at most this many RUNNING dispatches per sealed run at once, one per vendor by default; dispatch-run refuses a launch beyond it. Stale RUNNING transactions older than the wall-clock ceiling are ignored. Seats themselves cannot fan out: Claude seats launch with --disallowedTools Agent,Task and Codex seats with features.multi_agent=false (R12 enforced natively); agy has no equivalent flag, so a Gemini seat is bound by its contract and the scope audit only.",
    "requireCrossVendorReview": true,
    "requireObservedModelProof": true,
    "unknownAvailabilityIsUnavailable": true,
    "frontierEscalationOnly": true,
    "arbiterRetired2026-09-16": "xai/grok-4.6 retired as arbiter by owner instruction. The arbiter is the Jev decision engine (arbiter.decisionEngine); the hosting session (hostMode cursor-cli, synara or claude-code, declared by conclave-whoami) runs the tools and holds no vote. A plan declares arbiter {vendor: \"jev\", model: \"jev-latest\", host: \"<session slug>\"}; plan-seal records the Jev classification per unit and refuses a plan whose class Jev cannot support unless an owner override reason is recorded.",
    "catalogCulled2026-09-16": "Owner instruction: keep Astra and Sol (Codex), Fable and Opus (Claude), Gemini 3.1 Pro and Gemini 3.8 Flash (agy). Terra, Luna and Sonnet removed from every lane; Astra stays escalation-only where marked.",
    "checkingLanes2026-09-18": "Owner instruction 2026-09-18, both halves measured. (a) Four classes \u2014 debug-mystery, agentic-long-run, security-sensitive and extreme-end-to-end \u2014 had no verify or review lane, so work routed to them could be built and never checked; the last two also carry requiresPanel and were refused in every configuration, with checking seats ('no verify lane') and without them ('requires two independent review vendors'). Each now mirrors its own implement rung across all three vendors. (b) Opus refuses every CHECKING launch: cli-adapters adds --tools Read,Glob,Grep for non-implement roles only, completing the four-flag conjunction it declines, and Fable passes that identical launch. Opus keeps its lanes \u2014 it is a legal model and a classifier's reading of a launch shape is not a property of the model \u2014 but a Fable lane now sits ahead of it everywhere it checks, so the deterministic picker never chooses a seat that cannot start. Its implement lane carries no --tools restriction and is unaffected.",
    "arbiterVendorRecommendedDefault": "jev",
    "arbiterModelRecommendedDefault": "jev-latest",
    "arbiterAnyVendor": true,
    "arbiterIndependencePreferred": "independent",
    "arbiterPluggable2026-09-18": "Any vendor and model may arbitrate. arbiterVendor/arbiterModel are the RECOMMENDED default, not the only legal declaration: pinning them refused a plan for naming a different engine while hiding the question that matters, which is whether the arbiter scores replies from its own vendor. tools/arbiter-policy.js refuses exactly one arrangement - the arbiter's own vendor+model also holding a seat, since a model cannot score the independence of its own reply - and marks a run 'seated' when the arbiter merely shares a vendor with a seat. A seated run is legal and its bias is reported by tools/panel-stats.js --bias. Prefer an arbiter from a vendor that holds no seat: both arbiters on record (jev, xai) were independent, so there is NO measured baseline for a seated one.",
    "reviewLanes2026-09-18b": "standard-feature and bulk-mechanical had an implement lane and a verify lane and no review lane, so only one seat could ever vote on them against ORDINARY_QUORUM of 2: a plan sealed, and a perfect verify returned NOT_PANEL. The earlier checkingLanes pass fixed the four classes it was told about and left the two most ordinary ones. Each now mirrors its own verify lane. dispatch-matrix.test.js asserts the invariant rather than the instance: a class that can be built in must carry both checking lanes."
  },
